From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:18:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the view through strips in DTCM

Writing the view down the columns of the frame misses the data cache
with every pixel, which is slow in DS main RAM. The ray caster only
notes the texture column of each post and ScaleLine queues the sprite
columns over each column of the view instead. Once the weapon is queued
the view is put together in strips of 16 columns in DTCM: the ceiling
and floor filled in words, only the rows not every post of the strip
covers, so the screen isn't cleared first, then the wall posts and the
sprite columns over them, and each row of the strip is copied into the
frame as one burst of four words. The texture steps in 16.16 fixed
point, four pixels per loop with their loads first, as a branch costs
the ARM9 three cycles and a load the one after it. Posts taller than
the view are clipped at once.
---
 wl_def.h   |   8 ++++
 wl_draw.c  | 132 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 wl_scale.c |  79 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 166 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

